Make grpc++_unsecure visible outside the gRPC repository.

Orbit only ever creates insecure gRPC channels and servers -- every call site
uses InsecureChannelCredentials or InsecureServerCredentials -- so it links
grpc++_unsecure, the same target the pkg-config path in cmake/FindgRPC.cmake
selects. gRPC builds that target but keeps it behind an empty package group.

Linking the TLS stack instead would be worse than dead weight: gRPC's default
BoringSSL collides at link time with the OpenSSL that libssh2 brings in, and
building gRPC against OpenSSL instead makes the libraries Orbit injects into a
target process abort inside OpenSSL's initialisation, which runs in the fresh
linker namespace dlmopen creates.

--- a/BUILD	2026-08-21 01:43:11.821710835 -0700
+++ b/BUILD	2026-08-21 01:43:11.859413460 -0700
@@ -1264,7 +1264,7 @@
         "avoid_dep",
         "nofixdeps",
     ],
-    visibility = ["//bazel:grpc++_unsecure"],
+    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
     deps = [
